From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 07:46:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/28] flashnext: gather a shared pass's n-gram rows in one
 pool call and lock the tables' scales at load

A shared pass's gather thread takes every lane's rows in one pool call
(TF_FLASHNEXT_GATHER_EARLY=1, at most 64 lanes), each row still hashed after its own
stream's history, and an NVFP4 table's scale arrays can be mlocked at load
(TF_FLASHNEXT_GATHER_LOCK_SCALES=1) so a gathered row faults one page from disk, not two.
TF_FLASHNEXT_GATHER_LOG=1 prints what a shared pass launched ahead and waited at the PLE
layer, 100 passes a line.
